    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.tabline\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nIs there a way to hide the tabline when there is no tab open ?\r\n\r\nI tried to do an auto command but it didn't work:\r\n~~~lua\r\n    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"TabNew\", \"TabClosed\" }, {\r\n        desc = \"Hide the tabline when empty\",\r\n        group = group,\r\n        callback = function()\r\n            local show = #vim.api.nvim_list_tabpages() > 1\r\n            vim.opt.showtabline = show and 2 or 0\r\n        end,\r\n    })\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n`#vim.api.nvim_list_tabpages() > 1` seems to always return 1.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.tabline</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to hide the tabline when there is no tab open ?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tried to do an auto command but it didn't work:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ &quot;TabNew&quot;, &quot;TabClosed&quot; }, {\n        desc = &quot;Hide the tabline when empty&quot;,\n        group = group,\n        callback = function()\n            local show = #vim.api.nvim_list_tabpages() &gt; 1\n            vim.opt.showtabline = show and 2 or 0\n        end,\n    })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>({ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>TabNew<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>TabClosed<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}, {\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Hide the tabline when empty<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">group</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">group</span>,\n        <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n            <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">show</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">#</span><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_list_tabpages</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>\n            <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opt</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">showtabline</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">show</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n    })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">#vim.api.nvim_list_tabpages() &gt; 1</code> seems to always return 1.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.tabline\nQuestion\nIs there a way to hide the tabline when there is no tab open ?\nI tried to do an auto command but it didn't work:\n    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"TabNew\", \"TabClosed\" }, {\n        desc = \"Hide the tabline when empty\",\n        group = group,\n        callback = function()\n            local show = #vim.api.nvim_list_tabpages() > 1\n            vim.opt.showtabline = show and 2 or 0\n        end,\n    })\n#vim.api.nvim_list_tabpages() > 1 seems to always return 1.",
